The Book of Love
Why Love Makes You Powerful






Synopsis
I was taught that power belonged to others. That love was something to be earned. That to survive, I had to shrink myself. I was also conditioned to fight, relentlessly, for what I wanted. But I unlearned all of it. Or rather, I burned it all down.


Years of life altering challenges, microtraumas, unseen abuse, loss of power, loss of safety, and loss of direction led me to a complete collapse. This looked like a decade of progressively debilitating—yet functional—CPTSD that culminated in darkness and isolation. 


But from the ashes of grief, something spectacular happened. I burst outward—stronger, freer, more POWERFUL than ever before.


Like a supernova collapsing in on itself before birthing a star, here I was, changed.


LOVE and POWER came flooding to me, in their purest form, like precious and luminous gifts from within and from something larger than me.


So I was inspired to write this. 


The Book of Love is a radical, deeply personal, and fiercely insightful journey into spirituality, mysticism, and psychology—woven together with raw autobiographical experience, academic study, dedicated practice, and the kind of wisdom that only comes from truly living through it.


My message is simple: If the 2020s were the decade of self-love, the 2030s must be the decade of Love.


Not the love we’ve been sold—the conditional, the transactional, the exclusively me-oriented, the exclusivist, powerless and disempowering kind.


But the kind of LOVE THAT IS THE ULTIMATE POWER.


This book is a reclamation. Drawing from Buddhism, Jungian depth psychology, Gnostic teachings, Eastern philosophy, and mystical traditions, it explores Love in its most potent forms:


* The Love of Creation – The devotion of craftsmanship, artistry, and meaningful work.
* The Love of Self & Other – Reclaiming love in relationships, connection, and radical authenticity.
* The Love of Humanity – Compassion, service, and collective transformation.
* The Love of All-That-Is – The intelligence and passion poured into science, art, nature, and knowing all that can be known in the universe.
* The Love of God – Spiritual awakening, love of destiny, and transcendence.
* The Fierce Love – The kind that requires discipline, courage, and real self-work.


This is not a book about staying soft despite the pain you've endured. It’s not a trauma-dump either, a pop-psychology feel-good manual, or a book that vilifies those who cause harm. 


This is a book about radically reclaiming your right to Love and Be Loved Through themes like radical self-responsibility, the soul’s journey, and awakening to Love, this book will guide you toward an embodied understanding of your own power.


It’s time to let go of toxic individualism, limitations, and outdated paradigms.


It’s time to step into the flow of living from Power—where that POWER IS LOVE.


— Catalina




